  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2026  Portugal Floods contribution from Fedex</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">60 kVA power generators (diesel)
&#x2022; Suitable for continuous operation in emergency contexts
&#x2022; Compatible with:
o critical infrastructure;
o temporary shelters;
o operational bases;
o logistics platforms;
o medical and emergency response equipment.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">During the response to Storm Kristin, prolonged power outages were recorded in several areas, significantly affecting:
&#x2022; The operation of critical infrastructure;
&#x2022; The functioning of temporary shelters;
&#x2022; The continuity of humanitarian and logistical operations in the field.
To mitigate this situation, the Spanish Red Cross provided, on a loan basis, three 60 kVA generators, currently deployed at:
&#x2022; Pombal &#x2013; 2 units
&#x2022; Ansi&#xe3;o &#x2013; 1 unit
The prolonged duration of power outages and the high operational demand have clearly demonstrated the critical importance of this type of equipment to ensure operational continuity, population safety, and protection of field teams.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Immediate acquisition of three (3) 60 kVA power generators, aimed at reinforcing the Portuguese Red Cross (PRC) autonomous energy generation capacity within the framework of the response to Storm Kristin and the establishment of a national strategic emergency power reserve.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">People affected by the recent floods in Portugal</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022; Pombal &#x2013; 2 units
&#x2022; Ansi&#xe3;o &#x2013; 1 unit

And later to other disaster affected zones in Portugal</narrative>
  </description>
